# The `let _ = self.run_state_insert(...)` rollback in finish_run and
# fail_run_state is intentional: the primary error from the durable journal
# append is the one surfaced, and the rollback is a best-effort cleanup. The
# path-scoped `#[allow(clippy::let_underscore_must_use)]` documents the
# choice; without it the lint would force a bare expression statement which
# still triggers `unused Result that must be used`.
crates/vb_runtime/src/shard/transitions.rs|DISCARD-006|owner=holzman-rust|expiry=2026-12-31|follow_up=vb-ttki3|reason=best-effort rollback must drop the secondary Result; the primary journal-append error is what gets surfaced to the caller
